  "script": "Here's what happened to the last 12 Summer League MVPs in 2026. In 2014 it was Glen Rice Jr, but he only lasted two seasons in the NBA averaging about 27 points per game. 2015 Kyle Anderson, he currently plays for the Raptors, so far had a consistent bench career averaging roughly 7 points per game. 2016 Tyus Jones, he's currently a free agent, but his recent start really important, improving his game averaging close to 12 points per game. 2017 Lonzo Ball, had promising seasons derailed by knee injuries, most recently traded from the Cavs to the Jazz and the Jazz waived him, so he's currently not on an NBA team. 2018 Josh Hart, he became a high energy, high IQ, rebounding wing who was a crucial piece for that championship New York Knicks team. 2019 Brandon Clarke, thrived as an athletic big man for the Grizzlies and had a promising career, sadly he passed away this year may he rest in peace. 2020 had no Summer League because of COVID in the bubble. But to make up for it, 2021 had two MVPs. These Davion Mitchell and Cam Thomas, Davion gained a reputation as a defensive first guard. Thomas proven himself as a dynamic scorer with several 40 point games. 2022 Keegan Murray emerged as a dependable starter averaging roughly 12 points per game throughout his career. 2023 Cam Whitmore, currently plays for the Wizards, but in his first two seasons in Houston, he showed a lot of promise averaging over 10 points per game. 2024 Jalen Wilson, another promising player who just came off a 7 point per game season. 2025 Keyonte George is a really underrated combo guard who just came off a 12 point per game season for the Jazz. And in 2026, we have Jase Richardson of the Golden State Warriors, he is currently a rookie, hopefully he has a great career.",
